  "reason": "Evidence: The current best (config_020, acc=0.6352) uses pca_n2000 + imagenet_vit_l + avgpool + weighted. We've confirmed that multimodal >> image_only, avgpool > transformer, weighted ≥ concat, and pca_n2000 > scgpt (0.6287 vs 0.5176). The main untested dimension within the proven-best architecture is the RNA encoder: scvi_n2000 (a learned variational representation) has not been paired with the winning image encoder, aggregation, and fusion settings. This experiment tests whether scvi_n2000 can surpass pca_n2000 by capturing richer biological structure while keeping all other settings at their empirically best values. It is the best use of this slot because it directly extends the strongest configuration along the most impactful untested axis (RNA representation quality), and a positive result would immediately give a new best; a negative result confirms pca_n2000 is optimal and narrows the remaining 4 experiments to image-encoder or profile-setting variations. Expected relative cost: moderate (~6–7 GPU hours), comparable to config_020 (7.02) since it uses the same ViT-L backbone and weighted fusion, with scvi_n2000 likely similar in training overhead to scgpt."
}

